.TH FILE-CONFIG 3 "October 2026" "go-dhcpd 1.8.0" "go-dhcpd Plugin Interface"
.SH NAME
file-config \- read-only go-dhcpd config-provider plugin backed by config.json5
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I <install_prefix>/lib/go-dhcpd/plugins/file-config.plugin
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B file-config
is a go-dhcpd config-provider plugin, not a standalone command-line
program.
.B "It is not meant to be run directly from a shell."
It is spawned as a subprocess by
.BR dhcpd (8)
once per request: the daemon writes one JSON-encoded request to the
plugin's standard input and closes it, the plugin writes one
JSON-encoded response to standard output, and the process exits. See
.B PROTOCOL
below for the exact message shapes.
.PP
If
.B file-config
is executed interactively (standard input attached to a terminal), it
prints a warning explaining that it is a plugin and exits with status 1
instead of blocking on input; see
.B DIAGNOSTICS
below.
.PP
.B file-config
is
.BR read\-only :
it reports the
.B subnets
and
.B static
arrays already present in a go-dhcpd configuration file (by default the
daemon's own
.BR config.json5 (5),
or another file named by the
.B config_path
setting \(em see
.BR CONFIGURATION ),
reproducing go-dhcpd's original, pre-plugin behavior. Every
write action defined by the protocol is accepted but rejected with an
error response; it exists to preserve read access to file-based
configuration while the plugin architecture is adopted, not to make
that configuration mutable through the API. Use
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3)
instead for a plugin that supports create/update/delete operations.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.B file-config
is selected and configured through
.B plugins.config_provider
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5):
.PP
.RS
.nf
"plugins": {
  "config_provider": {
    "name": "file-config",
    "settings": { "config_path": "/etc/go-dhcpd/config.json5" }
  }
}
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BR config_path " (string, settings key)"
Path to the go-dhcpd JSON5 configuration file to read
.B subnets
and
.B static
from. When not explicitly set, the daemon defaults this to its own
configuration file's path, so omitting it reads the same file the
daemon itself was started with.
.SH PROTOCOL
Each invocation reads exactly one JSON request object from standard
input:
.TP
.B version
(integer) Protocol version; currently always 1.
.TP
.B action
(string) The operation requested; see
.B ACTIONS
below.
.TP
.B settings
(object) The plugin's configured settings, copied from
.B plugins.config_provider.settings
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.B data
(any, action-specific) Request payload; unused by every action
.B file-config
supports, since it never accepts new data to store.
.PP
Exactly one JSON response object is written to standard output:
.TP
.B status
(string) One of
.BR success " or " error .
.TP
.B message
(string, on error) A human-readable description of the failure.
.TP
.B data
(any, on success) Action-specific result payload.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B capabilities
Returns
.BR name ", " version ", and " writable
(always
.BR false ).
.TP
.B get_subnets
Returns the
.B subnets
array from the configuration file named by
.BR config_path ,
in the same shape documented under
.B SUBNETS
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5).
.TP
.B get_static_hosts
Returns the
.B static
array from the same file, in the shape documented under
.B STATIC
in
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5).
MAC addresses are normalized to lowercase.
.TP
.BR add_subnet ", " update_subnet ", " delete_subnet ", " add_static_host ", " update_static_host ", " delete_static_host
Rejected with a
.B status
of
.B error
and a message stating that the plugin is read-only. The go-dhcpd REST
API maps this to
.B 403 Forbidden
for the corresponding
.B /subnets
and
.B /static
write endpoints.
.PP
Any other
.B action
value is rejected with a
.B status
of
.B error
and an "unknown action" message.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
When standard input is a terminal (i.e. the binary was launched
directly by a user rather than by
.BR dhcpd (8)),
.B file-config
prints:
.PP
.RS
.nf
This binary is a go-dhcpd plugin (file-config).
These are not meant to be executed directly.
Please run go-dhcpd itself, which will invoke this plugin automatically.
.fi
.RE
.PP
to standard error and exits with status 1, without attempting to read a
request.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/go-dhcpd/plugins/file-config.plugin
Default install location (actual prefix depends on
.B INSTALL_PREFIX
used at build/install time; see
.BR dhcpd (8)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dhcpd (8),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-sqlite3\-config (3),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-config.json5 (5),
.BR go\-dhcpd\-migration\-tool (8)
